## Current implementation at M

The present `tools/graph.py:33-47` names/renders only CLAIMS.md, ROADMAP.md and
REVIEWS.md. Calling render(Repo()) returns precisely those three views, none a
witness ledger. `warrant/graph.py` offers around, path, why, frontier, delta and
impact queries; its actor frontier lists pending work and challenged own lineages,
not responsibility for refuted acceptances or replay credit. A search of the
current source, tests and docs found no witness-ledger implementation.
Thus the old ledger cannot be accepted as a functioning projection at M either.
Its generated Markdown leaving git in 97e33d11 was not the problem: that change
still rendered WITNESSES.md under build/views. The current renderer omits it.

